    "c_decisive_evaluate": "the single `evaluate` the shared harness/judge.py reads to decide the task, JSON-serialized. The decisive evaluate is the call whose returned payload the judge actually compares: for T6 that is the call that returned 'Hello Bench' on the new tab; for every other task the judge makes exactly one evaluate, so it is the last recorded call. Tasks whose judge reads a local file instead (T8/T9) make no evaluate call and their decisive representation cost is 0 tokens by construction."
